 heads. So, I want to know the probability of rolling a 7 with two six-sided dice.

Assistant: When rolling two six-sided dice, there are several combinations that can add up to a sum of 7:

- {1,6}
- {2,5}
- {3,4}
- {4,3}
- {5,2}
- {6,1}

There are 6 favorable outcomes out of a total of 36 possible outcomes (6 sides on the first die × 6 sides on the second die = 36).

The probability is therefore 6/36 or 1/6, which simplifies to a little under 17% chance each time you roll the pair of dice.

